      },
      "sellingPoints": [
        "Same claim, different channel: you change the structure, not the product story",
        "Every channel ships with its own hard rules (no links in the first Reddit paragraph, no pitch in cold email)",
        "Every edit is a version you can diff and roll back"
      ],
      "rawMaterial": "We had to say the same thing in six places every day. Copy-paste-edit turned into six contradictory drafts, and by v3 nobody remembered what v1 was about.\nSplitting \"the claim\" from \"the channel expression\" fixed it: one claim lives once, each channel gets its own draft and its own hard rules.",
